<!--
    A stated parameter a function hands on whole to a call is passed whole.
    P4 active-parameter trials (`p4_calls/kuna_wholeinputarg.rs`, no option).

    An AArch64 PLT veneer (adrp x16; ldr x17,[x16,#slot]; add x16; br x17)
    stated as `unsigned int veneer_int(struct Item *p)` passed its pointer to
    the indirect call cut to the return width: `(*dat_2000)((int4)p)`. The
    8-byte incoming x0 also has a 4-byte reader, the w0 of the stated return,
    so heritage splits the register and the call's trial covers only its low
    piece, read through heritage's own SUBPIECE of the input. The call took
    that piece either because the SUBPIECE passed the realistic-ancestor test
    or because fillinMap filled it as a hole below a later argument. Once the
    trials are mapped, a used trial that is such a piece of a parameter the
    caller's locked prototype states in that register takes the register.

    Hand-assembled (GNU as, linked at 0x1000, slots at 0x2000):
      veneer_int   unsigned int  (struct Item *p), slot 0x2000
      veneer_char  unsigned char (char *p),        slot 0x2008
      veneer_real  unsigned int  (unsigned int n), slot 0x2010
      veneer_long  long          (char *p),        slot 0x2018
      fwd    int (char *p, void *fp):          br x1
      two    int (char *p, long n, void *fp):  br x2
      zfwd   unsigned int (char *p, void *fp): mov w0,w0; br x1
      sfwd   unsigned int (char *p, void *fp): sxtw x0,w0; br x1
      zread  unsigned int (char *p, void *fp): add w2,w0,#1; br x1
      sfld   int (struct S { int a; int b; } s, void *fp): br x1
      vfmt   int (long u, long n): cbz w1; adr x0,"%d"; bl pr
      pr     int (char *f, ...): ret

    Assert #1 and #2: each veneer passes the whole pointer.
    Assert #3: so do the two tail calls through an untyped function pointer.
    Assert #4: no call passes p cut to a narrower integer.
    Assert #5 (control): a real 32-bit operand still passes 32 bits.
    Assert #6 (control): with an 8-byte return the register is not split, and
    no cut pointer appears (main passes nothing there).
    Assert #7 and #8 (controls): a zero or sign extension the code performs
    before the call is still passed.
    Assert #9: the pointer filled in below zread's later argument is whole.
    Assert #10 (control): a struct's first field passed on stays the field.
    Assert #11 (control): a variadic call keeps the int its format names.
    Assert #12: no cut of p hides behind SUB8x or a cast assigned to a local.

    No upstream issue. On the unpatched tree #1 to #4 and #9 fail and the
    rest pass; with the fix all twelve pass. #10 fails if the stated
    parameter's type is not checked, #11 if variadic calls are widened.
-->
